[{"_1":2,"_3":4},"root",{"_5":86},"routes/item",{"_5":6},"data",{"_7":8,"_9":10},"item",{"_11":12,"_13":14,"_15":16,"_17":18,"_19":-5,"_20":21,"_22":23,"_24":25,"_26":27,"_28":27,"_29":30,"_31":32,"_33":34,"_35":36,"_37":38,"_39":-5,"_40":-5,"_41":42,"_43":-5,"_44":45,"_46":47,"_48":49,"_50":51,"_52":36,"_53":54,"_55":-5,"_56":36,"_57":58},"expiresAt",1795048833000,"id","ln7qyvi7kwmhepx7dyfupziyv","title","Java4Shell、NGINX2Shell 等漏洞与 Microsoft 365 中断为何未触发 Infocon “Yellow”警报","originalTitle","Java4Shell, NGINX2Shell and more: Why we are not at \"Yellow\", (Wed, Nov 18th)","summary","SANS ISC 分析近期 Java、NGINX 严重漏洞及 Microsoft 365 中断为何未达到 Infocon “Yellow”警报标准。php2shell 漏洞此前已促使其向读者警示显著影响，但后续漏洞与事件的综合评估尚未达到触发该级别警报的门槛。","reason","source",{"_66":85},"links",{"_58":84},"publishedAt","2026-11-18T19:54:50.000Z","discoveredAt","2026-11-18T20:46:34.275Z","timelineAt","category","blue-team","tags",[80,69,71,81,82,83],"score",35,"selected",false,"channel","news","story","x","readingMode","full","author","body",{"_76":-5,"_58":77,"_78":-5,"_79":36},"outline",[],"relatedStories",[],"topics",[59,60,61,62,63],"indexable","markdownAvailable",true,"group","hasTranslation","bodyLanguage","original",{"_64":74,"_66":75},{"_64":72,"_66":73},{"_64":70,"_66":71},{"_64":68,"_66":69},{"_64":65,"_66":67},"slug","research","name","技术研究","vuln-mgmt","漏洞管理","incident","应急响应","oracle","Oracle / 甲骨文","microsoft","Microsoft / 微软","zh","<p>About a month ago, we went to Infocon Yellow for the first time in a few years. We decided to address the php2shell vulnerability and alert our readers to its significant impact. Following php2shell, we had a number of vulnerabilities and events that may also have scored high enough to trigger an Infocon \"Yellow\" [infocon]. In the last few days, we had a major Microsoft 365 outage, a critical vulnerability in Java, and a critical vulnerability in NGINX, which was disclosed today.</p>","zhKind","complete","汇总","Microsoft","Oracle","漏洞分析","https://isc.sans.edu/diary/rss/33532","SANS ISC",{"_87":88,"_89":-5},"changelogVersion","2026-10-01T08:00","release"]
